# Derived by hand from Semantics ch. 4 ("anywhere an expression is wanted, `@widget:` does"; a blueprint builds wherever it stands bare) and ch. 8 (a widget block is transparent: its places take the caller's next numbers): the local blueprint is built once per bare line. Under ruling PL a blueprint value applied is one place with one list: the local blueprint's label is that list's 0 (`0/0`, `1/0`).
